<section class="section" data-cart-page>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1 class="h1 mb-5">Your bag</h1>
    {% if cart.item_count > 0 %}
      <div class="grid cart-grid" style="--gap: var(--space-7);">
        <form action="{{ routes.cart_url }}" method="post" class="stack" style="--gap: var(--space-4);">
          {%- comment -%}
            ONE PRODUCT, ONE ROW - the same merge the drawer does, for the same
            reason, and it has to agree with the drawer or the bag reads
            differently depending on which one the shopper opened. The full
            explanation lives at the top of snippets/cart-drawer.liquid.

            THE noscript PATH STILL HAS TO ADD UP. updates[] is positional: one
            value per cart line, in cart.items order. A merged row renders one
            visible stepper carrying the variant's whole quantity, so the lines
            it swallowed each emit a hidden updates[] of 0 to hold their place
            in that sequence. Pressing "Update bag" with JavaScript off then
            performs exactly the merge the stepper performs with it on, rather
            than doubling the quantity.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign rendered_variants = '' -%}
          {% for item in cart.items %}
            {%- assign is_gift = false -%}
            {%- if item.properties['_free_gift'] -%}{%- assign is_gift = true -%}{%- endif -%}

            {%- assign skip_line = false -%}
            {%- unless is_gift -%}
              {%- comment -%}
            The key is the variant AND its properties. A personalised towel for
            Ada and one for Ela are the same variant and two different orders:
            merging them hid one name, and the stepper then wrote the hidden
            line to zero. Fragments of one split line share their properties,
            so they still merge. url_encode keeps the pipes a true delimiter
            whatever a shopper types as a name.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- capture vkey -%}|{{ item.variant_id }}{%- for prop in item.properties -%};{{ prop.first | url_encode }}={{ prop.last | url_encode }}{%- endfor -%}|{%- endcapture -%}
              {%- if rendered_variants contains vkey -%}
                {%- assign skip_line = true -%}
              {%- else -%}
                {%- assign rendered_variants = rendered_variants | append: vkey -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endunless -%}

            {%- if skip_line -%}
              <input type="hidden" name="updates[]" value="0">
            {%- else -%}
              {%- assign row_qty = item.quantity -%}
              {%- assign row_price = item.final_line_price -%}
              {%- assign merge_keys = '' -%}
{%- assign row_free = false -%}
              {%- unless is_gift -%}
                {%- assign row_qty = 0 -%}
                {%- assign row_price = 0 -%}
                {%- for other in cart.items -%}
                  {%- unless other.properties['_free_gift'] -%}
                    {%- capture other_vkey -%}|{{ other.variant_id }}{%- for prop in other.properties -%};{{ prop.first | url_encode }}={{ prop.last | url_encode }}{%- endfor -%}|{%- endcapture -%}
                    {%- if other_vkey == vkey -%}
                      {%- assign row_qty = row_qty | plus: other.quantity -%}
                      {%- assign row_price = row_price | plus: other.final_line_price -%}
{%- if other.final_line_price == 0 and other.original_line_price > 0 -%}{%- assign row_free = true -%}{%- endif -%}
                      {%- unless other.key == item.key -%}
                        {%- assign merge_keys = merge_keys | append: other.key | append: ',' -%}
                      {%- endunless -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endunless -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
              {%- endunless -%}

            <div class="cart-line{% if is_gift %} cart-line--gift{% endif %}" data-cart-line data-line-key="{{ item.key }}" style="padding: var(--space-4) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
              <a href="{{ item.url }}" class="cart-line__img"><img src="{{ item.image | image_url: width: 200 }}" alt="{{ item.product.title | escape }}" width="200" height="250"></a>
              <div>
                <a href="{{ item.url }}" class="cart-line__title">{{ item.product.title }}</a>
                {% unless item.variant.title contains 'Default' %}<div class="cart-line__variant">{{ item.variant.title }}</div>{% endunless %}
                {%- for prop in item.properties -%}
                  {%- assign prop_prefix = prop.first | slice: 0 -%}
                  {%- unless prop.last == blank or prop_prefix == '_' -%}
                    <div class="cart-line__prop">{{ prop.first }}: <strong>{{ prop.last }}</strong></div>
                  {%- endunless -%}
                {%- endfor -%}

                {%- if is_gift -%}
                  {%- comment -%}
                    No stepper on a gift - see cart-drawer.liquid. The quantity
                    still has to reach the form, so it goes in hidden and keeps
                    its place in the updates[] sequence.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <p class="cart-line__gift">{% if item.final_line_price > 0 %}Full price{% else %}Free gift{% endif %} &middot; 1</p>
                  <input type="hidden" name="updates[]" value="{{ item.quantity }}">
                {%- else -%}
                  {%- comment -%}
  The automatic discount makes one unit free whichever line it lands on, so a
  lip balm the shopper added themselves can drop to £0 with no gift picked.
  It stays a normal line with a stepper, because a second unit really is paid
  for; this only says why the price moved.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if row_free -%}<p class="cart-line__gift">{% if row_qty > 1 %}Includes your free gift{% else %}Free gift{% endif %}</p>{%- endif -%}
{%- assign line_max = item.product.metafields.custom.max_per_order.value | default: 5 -%}
                  {%- comment -%}
                    Product-wide, and gift lines excluded, exactly as the
                    drawer counts it. theme.js sums the steppers and a gift
                    line no longer has one, so this has to match or the note
                    and the button disagree.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  {%- assign product_total = 0 -%}
                  {%- for other in cart.items -%}
                    {%- unless other.properties['_free_gift'] -%}
                      {%- if other.product_id == item.product_id -%}
                        {%- assign product_total = product_total | plus: other.quantity -%}
                      {%- endif -%}
                    {%- endunless -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                  {%- comment -%}
  /cart/update.js takes any quantity with a 200 - four of a variant stocked at
  two, tested live on 6 November 2026 - and a merged row has to write through it.
  So a merged row carries what is left for it, after the variant's other lines
  including a gift, and theme.js holds the write to that. Blank means no limit.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign row_stock = '' -%}
{%- if merge_keys != blank and item.variant.inventory_management == 'shopify' and item.variant.inventory_policy == 'deny' -%}
  {%- assign row_stock = item.variant.inventory_quantity | plus: row_qty -%}
  {%- for other in cart.items -%}
    {%- if other.variant_id == item.variant_id -%}{%- assign row_stock = row_stock | minus: other.quantity -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- assign row_stock = row_stock | at_least: 0 -%}
{%- endif -%}
<div class="qty cart-line__qty" data-cart-qty data-line-key="{{ item.key }}" data-merge-keys="{{ merge_keys }}" data-stock="{{ row_stock }}" data-product-id="{{ item.product_id }}" data-max="{{ line_max }}">
                    <button type="button" data-cart-qty-dec aria-label="Decrease quantity">&minus;</button>
                    <input type="number" name="updates[]" value="{{ row_qty }}" min="0" max="{{ line_max }}" inputmode="numeric" data-cart-qty-input aria-label="Quantity for {{ item.product.title | escape }}">
                    <button type="button" data-cart-qty-inc aria-label="Increase quantity">+</button>
                  </div>
                  {%- comment -%}
                    Was rendered only when the line sat at its cap. It is now
                    always present, because the stepper writes into it when a
                    press of + cannot be honoured and needs somewhere to write.
                    Hidden while it has nothing to say, so the standing limit
                    still reads exactly as it did.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <p class="cart-line__limit" data-line-note data-line-key="{{ item.key }}" role="status"{% unless product_total >= line_max %} hidden{% endunless %}>
                    {%- if product_total >= line_max -%}
                      {%- if line_max <= 3 -%}Shipping weight limits this to {{ line_max }} per order.
                      {%- else -%}Limited to {{ line_max }} per order.{%- endif -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </p>
                {%- endif -%}
                <button type="button" class="cart-line__remove" data-cart-line-remove data-line-key="{{ item.key }}" data-merge-keys="{{ merge_keys }}">Remove</button>
              </div>
              <div class="cart-line__price">{{ row_price | money }}</div>
            </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {% endfor %}
          <noscript><button type="submit" name="update" class="btn btn-outline mt-3">Update bag</button></noscript>
        </form>
        <aside style="background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: var(--space-6); align-self: start; position: sticky; top: 100px;">
          <h3 class="h3 mb-4">Summary</h3>
          <div class="flow" style="--flow: var(--space-3);">
            <div class="cluster" style="justify-content: space-between;"><span class="muted">Subtotal</span><strong>{{ cart.total_price | money }}</strong></div>
            <div class="cluster" style="--gap: var(--space-3); justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: nowrap;"><span class="muted">Shipping</span><strong style="text-align: right;">{% assign free_ship_pence = settings.free_shipping_threshold | default: 25 | times: 100 %}{% if cart.total_price >= free_ship_pence %}Free{% else %}Calculated at checkout{% endif %}</strong></div>

            {%- comment -%}
              Same block the drawer uses. This page used to carry its own
              shipping bar and nothing about the gift, so a shopper who came
              via "View bag" reached checkout having never been told the gift
              exists - or that it cannot be combined with a discount code.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {% render 'cart-gift' %}

            <div class="cluster" style="justify-content: space-between; padding-top: var(--space-3); border-top: 1px solid var(--border);"><strong>Total</strong><strong style="font-size: var(--fs-xl);">{{ cart.total_price | money }}</strong></div>
            <a href="/checkout" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg btn-block">Checkout</a>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    {% else %}
      <div class="text-center" style="padding: var(--space-9) 0;">
        <p class="lead muted mb-4">Your bag is empty.</p>
        <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Continue shopping</a>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Cart main",
  "settings": [],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Cart main" }]
}
{% endschema %}
